    <string name="about_title">About Boris</string>
    <string name="about_back">Back</string>
    <string name="about_intro_title">Hello! I\'m Boris.</string>
    <string name="about_intro_body">I\'m a nostr-native app designed for reading and highlighting.</string>
    <string name="about_read_anywhere_title">Read Anywhere</string>
    <string name="about_read_anywhere_1">Boris works on any device. Whether you prefer to read on desktop, mobile, or tablet, Boris is there for you.</string>
    <string name="about_read_anywhere_2">Your highlights, bookmarks, and settings sync across devices over nostr, so you can pick up where you left off on phone, tablet, or desktop.</string>
    <string name="about_distraction_free_title">Distraction-Free</string>
    <string name="about_distraction_free_1">Boris aims to be a calm reader app with clean typography, beautiful design, and a focus on readability.</string>
    <string name="about_distraction_free_2">Boris does not and will never have ads, trackers, paywalls, subscriptions, or any other distractions.</string>
    <string name="about_airplane_mode_title">Airplane Mode</string>
    <string name="about_airplane_mode_1">Boris is offline-first by design. You can read, create highlights, and browse your library without a network. When offline, Boris stores changes locally and syncs later.</string>
    <string name="about_social_highlights_title">Social Highlights</string>
    <string name="about_social_highlights_1">Discover highlights from your friends and others, as well as long-form content from the nostrverse.</string>
    <string name="about_social_highlights_2">"Swarm highlights" help you discover the most interesting passages, while the feed shows you nostr-native long-form content.</string>
    <string name="about_lists_title">Lists, Libraries, and More</string>
    <string name="about_lists_1">Boris turns your bookmarks into a focused reading queue. It supports public and private bookmarks, regular web URLs, and RSS feeds.</string>
    <string name="about_lists_2">Keep track of reading progress, jump to specific passages, and mark articles (and other stuff) as read.</string>
    <string name="about_zap_splits_title">Zap Splits</string>
    <string name="about_zap_splits_1">When creating highlights, Boris automatically sets up zap splits so that value flows to authors and curators alike.</string>
    <string name="about_zap_splits_2">You have full control over all zap splits. You can change the splits as you wish or use one of the predefined presets.</string>
    <string name="about_comforting_colors_title">Comforting Colors</string>
    <string name="about_comforting_colors_1">Read during the day or late at night. Boris has multiple light and dark themes tuned for long reads. Choose fonts and sizes, highlight styles, and pick colors that fit your personal choice.</string>
    <string name="about_peace_of_mind_title">Peace of Mind</string>
    <string name="about_peace_of_mind_1">No signups, no accounts, no lock-ins. Your data lives on Nostr, and Boris renders it locally through an opinionated lens.</string>
    <string name="about_peace_of_mind_2">You will never be locked out, no matter what. You are in full control of your data. All the highlights, bookmarks, and reading metadata you create will always be available to you, if you care enough to keep them around.</string>
    <string name="about_free_title">Free as in Freedom</string>
    <string name="about_free_1">Boris is free and open-source and always will be. You can do with it what you want. Fork it, modify it, contribute to it, or just use it as is.</string>
    <string name="about_free_2_before">Boris is free as in beer too, but you can\u0020</string>
    <string name="about_free_2_link">send me sats</string>
    <string name="about_free_2_after">\u0020if you appreciate my work.</string>
    <string name="about_cta_title">Come say hi</string>
    <string name="about_cta_body">Connect on Nostr, or open GitHub to report a bug or suggest a feature.</string>
